{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/77648-killing-kindred-breaking-points","id":77648,"title":"Killing Kindred & Breaking Points","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-23T07:47:09-08:00","id":77648,"title":"Killing Kindred & Breaking Points","content":"Does killing Kindred or other supernatural creatures (werewolves, Geister, Prometheans, etc) count as &quot;murder&quot; for the purposes of breaking points on the Humanity chart, or does Humanity only apply to relating to <i>humans</i>? What about Kindred who are so degenerate that they bear at most a passing resemblance to humanity: Draugr, Stryx-possesed, etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1443-murderbunny","name":"Murderbunny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T09:10:04-08:00","id":77671,"title":"","content":"Killing kindred when you ARE a kindred is certainly something that would shake your sense of humanity. Killing something you might one day become would be as well. These are not things your average human would do. If your justifying it in some way or another, it basically means you've lost humanity. Humanity is basically how human you feel, how much you relate back with humanity is only part of it. If your running around killing others like yourself, or running around fighting 'monsters' how much of a normal human does that feel like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T09:46:00-08:00","id":77696,"title":"","content":"Killing monstrous or degenerate vampires, no. But killing George, that nice guy who does the Prince's computer security and embarrassedly confessed to you that one time that he still hasn't killed anyone and never wants to? <br /> <br /> Definitely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T09:54:00-08:00","id":77700,"title":"","content":"I'd say killing monstrous vampires is, hell, probably SEEING monstrous vampires is a breaking point for humanity. It isn't about morality, its about how it makes you feel in relation to humanity. Now, these might be higher than murder when they're Draugr or Larvae, (5-6 tops, I'd argue it would be more around 4 because its more equivalent to impassioned killing, and still not a normal human thing to be doing).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T10:53:40-08:00","id":77735,"title":"","content":"I would agree with Rani that meeting a Draugr should be a Breaking Point, but the severity of it would probably vary a lot. I think different Kindred would react very differently to such an encounter, for some it is a reminder of what they are and might become for some it is a confirmation of what they are <b>not</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T11:37:07-08:00","id":77753,"title":"","content":"I don't see degeneracy as really having anything to do with it, anymore than killing a degenerate human. I'm pretty much with Saibot on this; otherwise whacking other Kindred should most certainly be a breaking point. These are the only people who can empathise and understand you and your state fully. They are what you could be, or what you could become. Going out of your way to whack your social circle who are in an extended way a mirror of yourself because you find them -horrible-... that should most certainly distance you from Humanity. Obviously it rocks your boat enough to take an extreme risky action.<br /> <br /> Them being good or bad individuals may alter what level of Humanity the Breaking Point is, but I think it should remain one nonetheless. Kindred are individuals. People are individuals. Few in the world are saints, they're exceptions for a reason (and even some of those saints may not be all that great of folks...) going off and whacking them and validating it as not being murder is semantics bordering on sociopathy. It's not what a sane human consistently does, and even then it is a slippery slope. It's not considered acceptable in most societies without high levels of social ritual (and even then it's hotly contested) barring self-defense, and even then that runs into issues. How is doing that do your own kind and peers somehow less worse?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T12:38:29-08:00","id":77782,"title":"","content":"That makes sense: Kindred are human enough that killing them is a lot like killing a human, except perhaps for the types that are more like ambulatory repositories for the Beast (Draugr, Strix). Encountering a Draugr as a breaking point makes sense to me, but I think it should be pretty high, in the 8-10 range along with the other reminders of one's inhuman state: inability to eat food or walk outside in the sun, the ability to endure injuries that would tear mere mortals to pieces. <br /> <br /> What about other creatures: a rampaging werewolf in Gauru (hybrid monster) form, a lumbering Frankenstein's Monster?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1443-murderbunny","name":"Murderbunny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T13:11:52-08:00","id":77795,"title":"","content":"I would say it depends on how much the vampire in question understands of these beings. Putting down a rampaging werewolf is basically like putting down a rabid beast, unless you know this is not their normal state of being and they have a quite complex society themselves. Killing a Promethean is as bad as killing a normal human, unless you know what they are or are suffering a Disquiet Frenzy, in which case it is a slightly softer Breaking Point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T21:33:40-08:00","id":78070,"title":"","content":"I would count all the playable character types as human for purposes of breaking points. You can move a breaking point up as a sin for certain circumstances, inhuman shape or a degenerate mental state. I think of it like this: A serial killer is still human. Most people would balk at killing a murderer unless it was for self-preservation. It would likely be a &quot;breaking point&quot; even then. I would move most vampires up a notch and draugr one more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T12:00:37-08:00","id":78481,"title":"","content":"I'd err on the side of it being a breaking point; even with the most savage and far-gone vampires, once you kill the one, it becomes immediately apparent that they were at least human once. If you imagine the guy who kills a ravaging vampire and can still look down at the withering corpse and spit in its eye, that's not someone who didn't hit a breaking point, it's someone who passed his roll at the breaking point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1358-polisurgist","name":"Polisurgist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T12:50:02-08:00","id":78518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Polisurgist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/77648-killing-kindred-breaking-points?p=78481#post78481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd err on the side of it being a breaking point; even with the most savage and far-gone vampires, once you kill the one, it becomes immediately apparent that they were at least human once. If you imagine the guy who kills a ravaging vampire and can still look down at the withering corpse and spit in its eye, that's not someone who didn't hit a breaking point, it's someone who passed his roll at the breaking point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that was the guy who FAILED the breaking point, rather than passing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T12:55:15-08:00","id":78522,"title":"","content":"Certainly. If you succeed you realize the wrong of your actions but still hold yourself together.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T14:01:12-08:00","id":78568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/77648-killing-kindred-breaking-points?p=78518#post78518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'd say that was the guy who FAILED the breaking point, rather than passing it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, that's the kind of reaction I would narrate for a dramatic failure. A failure is being able to justify it to yourself. spitting in the eye of a victim you recognize as at least having once been human is a step beyond, that's some serious degeneration into jaded monstrousness. A success would be realizing that even though it looked like a monster, killing it was still wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T16:05:02-08:00","id":84905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/77648-killing-kindred-breaking-points?p=78518#post78518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say that was the guy who FAILED the breaking point, rather than passing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was basically thinking &quot;this guy doesn't walk away from it with a Condition,&quot; but yeah...the important thing is that this is someone who had to make a roll, not someone whose player convinced the ST that it wasn't really murder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1358-polisurgist","name":"Polisurgist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T11:06:42-08:00","id":826950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murderbunny</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes sense: Kindred are human enough that killing them is a lot like killing a human, except perhaps for the types that are more like ambulatory repositories for the Beast (Draugr, Strix). Encountering a Draugr as a breaking point makes sense to me, but I think it should be pretty high, in the 8-10 range along with the other reminders of one's inhuman state: inability to eat food or walk outside in the sun, the ability to endure injuries that would tear mere mortals to pieces.<br /> <br /> What about other creatures: a rampaging werewolf in Gauru (hybrid monster) form, a lumbering Frankenstein's Monster?</div> </div> </div> </div>I find myself agree with this post. I also think it could easily be a breaking point to leave horrible monsters alive if you have the power to do something about them, either to end their suffering, or the suffering they cause. It may be a breaking point to kill them, but <i>not</i> killing them could result in repeated breaks when you're confronted with their suffering or wake of their carnage. It's like having to yank off the bandage to avoid it getting septic, painful but worth it in the long run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T05:16:17-08:00","id":827426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Polisurgist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/77648-killing-kindred-breaking-points?p=84905#post84905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was basically thinking &quot;this guy doesn't walk away from it with a Condition,&quot; but yeah...the important thing is that this is someone who had to make a roll, not someone whose player convinced the ST that it wasn't really murder.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's actually impossible to walk away from a humanity check without a condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T07:09:00-08:00","id":827485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PrinceRaven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/77648-killing-kindred-breaking-points?p=827426#post827426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's actually impossible to walk away from a humanity check without a condition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Pretty sure they meant 'negative condition'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T08:26:14-08:00","id":827532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/77648-killing-kindred-breaking-points?p=77671#post77671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Killing kindred when you ARE a kindred is certainly something that would shake your sense of humanity. Killing something you might one day become would be as well. These are not things your average human would do. If your justifying it in some way or another, it basically means you've lost humanity. Humanity is basically how human you feel, how much you relate back with humanity is only part of it. If your running around killing others like yourself, or running around fighting 'monsters' how much of a normal human does that feel like?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I agree with this. Too many players think of Humanity as morality. They are indeed closely related. Killing anything at all is a breaking point. It doesnt specify humans... if you want to justify it and make it so you dont have to roll for killing vampires... that's what banes are for. If you know you are going to be off fighting the bad werewolves and killing them, then take a bane. <br /> <br /> I personally think that it would be MORALLY wrong to leave a crazy werewolf/vampire alive to run a muck, I dont think it would break your humanity. Most humans dont feel the need to for vigilante justice, they leave the monster hunting for the... Hunters. Also if you feel guilty( moral problem) about their actions.. there are other resolutions besides death. <br /> <br /> Humanity is meant to be how human you feel.. how attached to the mortal world you are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T22:20:43-08:00","id":828007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/77648-killing-kindred-breaking-points?p=827485#post827485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure they meant 'negative condition'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, pass or fail you're getting a negative condition unless you rolled an exceptional, which is fairly unlikely considering murder is a check at 1-2 dice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9368-princeraven","name":"PrinceRaven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T06:43:16-07:00","id":848756,"title":"","content":"Killing a normal vampire is the same as killing a mortal.<br /> <br /> Killing a draugr might be the same as impassioned killing even if it's premeditated, as long as the killer is in the right frame of mind. Witnessing a draugr being itself and realizing that is one of your possible futures, especially if it's the first time, is probably a breaking point on it's own, a Humanity 5-ish perhaps?<br /> <br /> I'd say that killing a strix is at most a Humanity 4 breaking point, like impassioned violence or accidentally killing a human. Striges are very much a Other that never was quite human in the first place. (Killing a host in the process would be a separate roll, of course)<br /> <br /> For Mr. crazy werewolf it depends on how much the vampire knows/understands about the situation. If the leech research preperly and comes up with a murder plot it's like killing a human. If it's just a matter of &quot;OHGOD WHAT'S THAT RAMPAGING THING KILLIT KILLIT KILLIT WITH FIRE NO I DON'T CARE IT'S FIRE HE'S WORSE!!!&quot; [after a frenzied fight] &quot;OK. Silver, uh? So... werewolves are a thing?&quot; it's probably a Humanity 4 one because the vampire doesn't quite realize the implications.<br /> <br /> <br /> An addendum: I would accept considering two instances of killing other vampires as only one breaking point for one single bane (impassioned and premeditated but not accidental, for example) as long as it applies only to vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1866,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","user":"Ophion","date":". 03-17-2016, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","name":"Ophion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T07:58:11-07:00","id":848793,"title":"","content":"I feel like it's ridiculously hard to actually kill a vampire, rather than just put one in torpor. Torporing a vampire should never be below a 4 (for impassioned violence--note it doesn't say killing), and sometimes could be higher for self-defense type stuff. But actually finishing that helpless, torpored vampire? That's murder. You're ending someone who is no threat to anyone. Even if they're a draugr, they would just look like a regular, helpless person when torpored. That's humanity 2, at best. <br /> <br /> It's extremely difficult and unlikely that you torpor and final death a vampire in a single action, though if the unlikely were to happen, I'd still go with 4, since you never have to deal with the helpless, motionless body you know won't be awake for days (possibly centuries) just lying there waiting for your coup de grace.<br /> <br /> As for other templates, that's different. They don't all have that &quot;helpless but not dead without further intervention&quot; state, so, I wouldn't treat them differently than I would a human. You're almost certainly getting self-defense bonuses for a raging Garou, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}